The issue is that the `RST` class does not accept `header_rows` in its `__init__` method, which causes a `TypeError` when `tbl.write(..., header_rows=...)` is called. While the issue description shows a failure during `write`, the provided test failure shows a failure during `read`. 

In `astropy.io.ascii`, `header_rows` is passed to the `Writer` class during `write()` and to the `Reader` class during `read()`. The `RST` class is a `Writer`. The `RST` class inherits from `FixedWidth`, which in turn inherits from `ascii.ascii.core.BaseWriter`. 

The `RST` class needs to accept `**kwargs` in its `__init__` to avoid the `TypeError` when additional arguments (like `header_rows`) are passed.

